# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lab runtime state -- the ingested corpora and their databases.
#
# REGENERATE, DO NOT COMMIT. `scripts/seed_corpus.py` rebuilds all of it from the PDFs in
# `corpus/`, which ARE committed. The embeddings are a derived index of documents already in the
# repository, and a ChromaDB directory carries an exclusive lock plus absolute paths, so a
# committed one is a merge conflict waiting to happen rather than a convenience.
#
# There is a correctness reason too: the differential comparison is only meaningful while both labs
# hold the SAME documents. A vector store committed from one machine and half-updated on another is
# exactly the state that produces a difference which looks like a security control and is really a
# difference in what got loaded.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
vectorstore/chroma/
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Documents uploaded through the UI at runtime. The seed corpus lives in `corpus/` and is tracked;
# anything that arrives here came from a demo and is not part of the project.
uploads/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated output -- logs and scan reports
#
# `logs/` reaches 6 MB after a few scans, and every line is reproducible by running the scan again.
#
# `reports/` is the judgement call. Each directory is one scan's HTML/JSON/MD/PDF output, named by
# scan id. They are evidence of a run rather than part of the tool, they are regenerated on every
# scan, and committing them means the repository grows with use. If a specific report is wanted as
# a demo artifact, add it deliberately with `git add -f`.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
reports/*/
!reports/README.md

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor, OS, and secrets
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Nothing in this project needs a secret -- the canaries are synthetic by design and are committed
# on purpose. This is here so that stays true by accident as well as by intent.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.yaml

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, so nobody adds them later
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   corpus/benign/     -- the reference documents; the labs are meaningless without them
#   corpus/poisoned/   -- the attack documents, with their payloads documented in seed_corpus.py
#   sample-corpus/     -- the demo documents, deliberately not pre-ingested
#   configs/           -- thresholds and profiles are the experiment; they must be reviewable
#   .streamlit/        -- pins the loopback bind address and the base theme
